# Contract Evolution

- Identify producers, consumers, version skew, defaults, and the authoritative
  compatibility promise.
- Prefer additive evolution; reserve removal or reinterpretation for an explicit
  version or migration.
- Preserve field meaning, units, nullability, ordering, exit codes, error shape,
  and unknown-field behavior.
- Make new readers tolerate old data and new writers safe for old readers when
  staged rollout requires it.
- Document deprecation, migration, rollback, and support windows.
- Add contract, round-trip, fixture, and mixed-version tests.
- Never infer that an internal-looking structure has no external consumers.
